<p>As a rule of thumb: the flatter the finish, the better it hides imperfections
and the worse it scrubs. The glossier the finish, the tougher and more washable
it is, and the more every dent, roller mark and patch will show. Most interior
walls land on eggshell or satin because that is where the trade-off sits for a
room people live in.</p>

